        {
          "title": "Medal of Honor - Infiltrator",
          "longTitle": "Medal of Honor - Infiltrator (USA, Europe) (En,Fr,De)",
          "type": "gba",
          "background": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webrcade-assets/webrcade-assets-gba-images/master/Named_Snaps/output/Medal%20of%20Honor%20-%20Infiltrator%20(USA%2C%20Europe)%20(En%2CFr%2CDe).png",
          "thumbnail": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webrcade-assets/webrcade-assets-gba-images/master/Named_Titles/resized/Medal%20of%20Honor%20-%20Infiltrator%20(USA%2C%20Europe)%20(En%2CFr%2CDe).png",
          "description": "Medal of Honor Infiltrator is a shooter from a top-down viewpoint. The top-down graphics and gameplay are reminiscent of classic games like Commando and Frontline.\n\nIn its 15 total levels, Infiltrator brings together a variety of different play styles that should be familiar to anyone who's played their fair share of 8- and 16-bit games. \n\nYou can hide behind houses and other buildings to stop enemy bullets.\nIf you come across a stationary gun or a tank sitting in a level, you can put these weapons to use against the enemy.\n \nEach level has a number of mission objectives assigned to it, such as locating documents or destroying ammunition depots. To complete a level, you need to accomplish these goals. \n\nThe difficulty level is, like its forerunners, high and urges the players all the time.",
